{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "home-assistant",
  "description": "A realistic Home Assistant install: eleven entities of which only four carry an address, and a device registry holding six entries of which four are real network hardware. Entity payload shapes follow the State._as_dict serialization in home-assistant/core (entity_id, state, attributes, last_changed, last_reported, last_updated, context) and the ScannerEntity attribute keys ip/mac/host_name, with UniFi's raw client fields (oui, ap_mac, essid, vlan) riding along as extra_state_attributes. Timestamps use the +00:00 offset form Home Assistant actually emits - never Z - and one deliberately omits the fractional part, which is what happens when the microsecond is zero. This is the scenario that proves the scope decision: automations, the sun, a light, a temperature sensor, a legacy tracker with no MAC, a Zigbee bulb whose only connection is an IEEE address, and a cloud service entry are all skipped, while the access point, camera, smart plug, printer, phone, and absent laptop are imported. It also proves entity claiming - the printer's device_tracker entity enriches the registry device rather than becoming a second asset, which would be permanent because two foreign ids from one integration can never merge onto one asset.",
